# expect: 34
# tags:   goal_out, goal_alive, gravity, stuck, tier30
# why:    the item has to go out on the right, so the fish - starting right
#         beside it - must swim the long way round, over the wall, to get to its
#         left. The obvious move, pushing it left, drops it into a one-wide
#         pocket in the floor where it can never move again: no fish fits
#         beside or below it. The fish is goal_alive, so the walled-in-fish rule
#         says nothing; only the goal_out half of the stuck-item rule (docs/020)
#         sees that the item will never leave. The walls-only item distance lets
#         items be lifted and ignores the fish's detour, so those dead states
#         sit far below the optimum and plain A* searches every one of them.
# s: fish_small < goal_alive
# A: item_light goal_out
